The function below is the correct version of a scan that returns the length of the longest subarray with at most two distinct values. The array is `X = [1, 2, 1, 2, 3, 3, 3, 2]`. What does it return?
```c
int first=0, second=0, len1=0, len2=0, maxlen=0;
for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
  if (X[i] == first) { len2++; len1++; }
  else if (X[i] == second) { len2++; len1 = 1; second = first; }
  else { len2 = len1 + 1; len1 = 1; second = first; }
  if (len2 > maxlen) maxlen = len2;
  first = X[i];
}
```
